 "notes": "Endpoints: the committed OpenAPI 3 spec (spec/api.json) plus routes verified in the code while checking extracted items (public redirect twins of the admin routes, GET on the self-service submit paths, the OIDC callbacks, /admin/health/config); the two /self-service/fed-cm routes are only in the spec (no registration in this code) and were removed. Scope: the packages that register the public/admin APIs. Findings: (1) const-concat — a route constant built from another constant, RouteItem = RouteCollection + \"/{id}\", keeps only the literal tail (/{id}); this is an extractor defect, not a missing feature. (2) prefix-in-router-type — RegisterAdminRoutes(admin *httprouterx.RouterAdmin): the admin router type prepends /admin (AdminPrefix, in the vendored ory/x) to everything it registers. (3) const-in-format: fmt.Sprintf(\"/%s/{id}\", SchemasPath). (4) route-in-loop: public.Handle(m+\" \"+RouteWhoami, h) for m in a list of methods. When a route needs const-concat and the /admin prefix, it is counted as const-concat. Test helpers outside _test files (pkg/testhelpers, courier/template/testhelpers) register routes (test-app-folder). Calls: the OIDC providers (selfservice/strategy/oidc/), literal URLs only — the ones built on url.Parse(issuer) + u.Path = path.Join(...) are url-object-builder, URLs kept in struct fields set by the constructor are url-in-field, a package var is url-in-var. pkg/httpclient and pkg/client-go are two copies of the openapi-generator Go client of spec/api.json (localVarPath := localBasePath + \"/self-service/...\", the verb in localVarHTTPMethod, sent by prepareRequest): since H2b item 7 for Go (2026-10-16) the spec's 60 operations are expected calls (via generated-client), and both copies give all 60. The url-object-builder ones come out since the same change. Since the v2 cheap fixes (2026-10-15) constants built from constants resolve (const-concat is fixed): routes still missed because of the /admin router type are now prefix-in-router-type. The LinkedIn provider's GET /v2/me and /v2/emailAddress (package constants passed to its own fetch helper) were missing from this list and were added; they come out as ANY. Since H2 Phase 5 (2026-10-17): testhelpers/ folders are test code, so the fake servers there left (GET /{filename} was in the sample, test-app-folder); fmt.Sprintf(\"/%s\", SchemasPath) takes the one-segment constant, so schema/handler.go gives GET /schemas and /schemas/{id} (const-in-format).",
